      "metadata": {
        "id": "reflected-garage"
      },
      "source": [
        "The accuracy of the model on the test and validation set are above 84%, which suggests that our model generalizes well to data it hasn't seen before. But how good is 84% accuracy? While this depends on the nature of the problem and on business requirements, a good way to verify whether a model has actually learned something useful is to compare its results to a \"random\" or \"dumb\" model.Let's create two models: one that guesses randomly and another that always return \"No\". Both of these models completely ignore the inputs given to them."
      ]
